  "cannot_show": ["Human:rat mixing of real DNA is untested: only human:mouse real mixtures exist, so step 1 validates the in-silico procedure for mouse and its transfer to rat is assumed.", "The rat reference (GSE174568, EpigenDx standard; liver per component sheets; strain and lot unknown) is not RNU/RNU brain, and it was run on other chips in another lab; the f = 0 end of the curve is measured only off our chip, which is where N2 lies.", "f is a share of haploid genome copies under the scaling rule; GEO fractions are presumably by DNA mass; neither is a cell fraction, and U251 is aneuploid.", "U251 copy-number change in vivo, rat strain variants under probes, and cross-hybridisation below AS 35 enter the tumour arrays but the curve only through the rat arrays' own background.", "Calibrated reading (Amendment 1): phi is measured on human blood with mouse spleen or fat on two other chips; that the same phi holds for human:rat, for U251 DNA and on our chip is assumed. phi is steepest at low f, where it rests on the 0.05 and 0.1 mixtures (0.05 in batch 2 only), which is N2's range."],
